{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"body":"## Operator-ratified decision (2026-08-04) — recorded before implementation\n\nGold-aware ASYMMETRIC scoring for the parity bar's criterion (b): on an arm\ndisagreement over a gold-labelled item, consult the gold label. A candidate\nmust NEVER be failed for agreeing with gold against the baseline.\n\nConcretely:\n- A decision flip where the CANDIDATE matches gold and the baseline does not\n  is a gold-IMPROVING flip — it must not count against the zero-flip gate.\n- A flip where the candidate moves AWAY from gold (baseline matched gold, or\n  neither matches but candidate diverges from gold) remains a gating failure\n  as before.\n- Agreement cases are unchanged.\n- Missing/absent gold label: behaviour preserved (non-gold pairs were never\n  in the flip count; the agreement floor treatment is decided during\n  implementation and documented).\n\nHard constraint: validation via unit tests over recorded/fixture verdicts\nonly — zero live LLM calls; no full eval sweeps."},"env_id":"ade0f2ef-51cc-45a2-bb97-c09846cd3df5","event_type":"COMMENT","timestamp":1785862528539610001,"uuid":"09a68665-f7a6-496b-92fd-48da37177a56"}